# Robot 1 v1: it fits the size rules, the intake drops at START and stays down, the intake and the
# launcher answer the buttons, and a held piece is fired.
# Run it (from the ftc-helper-lib folder):  ./gradlew :sim:scenario -Pfile=../simulator/scenarios/r1-v1.sim
robot ../robot.properties
init "R1 TeleOp"
expect size start ok                   # folded: inside the 18 in cube
expect size most ok                    # every pose: 18 x 24 x 29 in
expect size floor ok
expect shape intake_arm = 95 0.1       # folded up
start
expect within 3 shape intake_arm = -40 0.1    # pushed over: down on its stop
expect within 3 servo intake_deploy actual < 0.05   # the servo went back
expect shape intake_arm = -40 0.1      # and the intake stays down
expect size match ok                   # deployed: 18 x 24 x 29 in
set preload off                        # start empty, so the pick-up below is a real one
expect stored = 0
set piece POLLEN -56 -50                # a POLLEN 11 in ahead of the robot
hold g1.right_trigger                  # intake in
expect within 1 motor intake power > 0.9
hold g1.left_stick_y -0.4              # drive forward onto it
expect within 3 stored >= 1
release all
expect within 1 motor intake power = 0 0.01
press g1.left_bumper                   # spin the flywheel up
expect within 4 motor launcher velocity > 1100
press g1.right_bumper                  # fire one
expect within 3 launched >= 1
print size
stop
expect error none
